Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["The Breathless Line", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Reviewed by Pavel Hajek.", "TI"]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29195e13-f070-4eda-87ea-ef3991911312"],

Cell["\<\
Euclid describes a line as a \"breadthless length\". Every line we draw has \
some thickness; a line without breadth belongs to an idealized geometry. We \
ask whether such an ideal object can emerge from a discrete substrate: can a \
family of shortest paths, spread across a graph, concentrate on a straight \
segment as the graph is refined?\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1f8ac89e-c67a-4531-a1ab-2a41d86703ed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To make this precise, start with a graph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ce29c7b1-9027-46f2-88f5-6a65b8a551f8"],
 " embedded in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\:211d", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0dc27d17-f84f-4bc3-b3ee-0ae22fdd03e6"],
 " and specify how it is subdivided. For a triangular mesh, we can consider \
barycentric subdivision and write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], "0"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a111b7a0-2349-4009-a077-e8dcb23ba921"],
 ". The original endpoints remain fixed, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed1e0719-f83f-4e12-841b-4c7f421e9756"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c5722c25-0436-45d9-b7b8-30095f93fedd"],
 ", while the minimal model ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["l", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b9f99547-3b02-4a65-8a45-c54a057fc398"],
 " may contain many shortest paths."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"62feabe3-7058-4235-9d1c-3bf2ce078cbb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each subdivision inherits an embedding. Counting the paths through each \
edge or vertex gives an occupation density. We ask whether its normalized \
measure converges weakly to uniform length on the straight segment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "61d64448-f19a-4c73-a2a9-2f3101fa4110"],
 ", and how quickly its transverse spread vanishes."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"df4a356c-f154-454f-adb5-d08add26acc8"],

Cell["\<\
The regular triangular tessellation provides a natural comparison: does it \
have the same convergence rate, or is it special in some way?\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fc469c43-319b-4f01-b734-778f8dbead18"],

Cell["\<\
Instead of barycentric subdivision, we can also consider midpoint refinements \
of square and triangular grids.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a0229be0-1bd9-433b-99cb-20987dcc7bdc"],

Cell["\<\
For the hexagonal tessellation, we first need to decide what refinement \
should mean.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1e475116-201d-4f6e-8928-5c6ee9d31a57"],

Cell["\<\
Now we will try to formulate the problem without a fixed embedding.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"def34ef2-3339-48cf-9158-e8c1dc027191"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5a92713c-1363-47e1-bc57-fa1c2fcc978d"],

Cell["\<\
Barycentric subdivision comes from the DiscreteGeometry paclet.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"43f2ad4d-39e0-4629-a712-d843a7536940"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`InfraGeometry`\>\"", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`DiscreteGeometry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"37a30d36-a104-4bdf-91f2-8f9a88791575"],

Cell["Paths and occupation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"90741ae1-d7e2-4e7f-acec-8ca894cbdb28"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c0b481d-f81a-4007-b37d-bfa22d537027"],
 " be distinct vertices of a finite unweighted graph. Suppose there are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["N", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0eb81b0-dd75-48f1-8698-8ad2e3f02d5e"],
 " shortest paths between them, each with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "225257fd-bdc2-493f-8532-90d766915ffd"],
 " edges."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26545cdb-5fd6-43a7-a346-44c86be6c01b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["E", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8ea295c0-d06c-41f2-819e-906c9dc20c22"],
 " for the number of these paths containing edge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["e", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05dd1e9f-a61f-4131-a3fb-c1a617c18622"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f726c1d-5c0f-4a6a-891c-8fd8f9ae601c"],
 " for the number containing vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["v", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "abded53d-c214-4fe6-88f7-5c39d71d8373"],
 ". Each path contributes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8245deea-955b-4300-8dbf-b9e62355dac6"],
 " edge visits and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04e6d08c-ff5f-4228-8753-a892fb27b4f4"],
 " vertex visits, so"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"19b947aa-2267-43b4-8c43-d20695bef88a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  FrameBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      StyleBox["e", "TI"],
      LimitsPositioning->False], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["E", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
     StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]}], ",", 
    "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       StyleBox["v", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["V", "TI"]], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["L", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}]}]],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"a53dcc77-357f-4a57-\
b04b-547ffbad95df"],

Cell["\<\
For example, the two-square grid below has three shortest paths from a to b, \
each of length three. The edge labels are the occupation counts; they sum to \
nine.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"da980b55-be06-4c15-aad7-ee377b3602f4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"GridGraph", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"counts", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"InfraMeasurement", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"InfraSegment", "[", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", "\"\<EdgeDensity\>\""}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Graph", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"InfraSubstrateHighlight", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"InfraSegment", "[", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
          "StandardBlue"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
          "StandardBlue"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"EdgeLabels", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"KeyMap", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"UndirectedEdge", " ", "@@", " ", "#"}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
         " ", "counts"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"VertexLabels", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Placed", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", ",", " ", "Before"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"6", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Placed", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<b\>\"", ",", " ", "After"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"21bdfeca-560d-44aa-8768-d91a2b12ceab"],

